<Layout title="Privacy — Rycode" description="How Rycode handles a visit.">
  <article class="plain-page">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p>Rycode is a static site. It does not ask you to create an account, and it does not sell personal information.</p>
    <p>The host may keep ordinary server logs, such as the address of a request, so the site can stay online. These pages do not set their own tracking cookies.</p>
    <p>Some links leave this site. <a href="https://systems.rycode.dev" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Systems<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a> is one of them.</p>
    <p>Questions go to <a href="/contact/">Contact</a>.</p>
  </article>
</Layout>
